WEBVTT

00:00:06.890 --> 00:00:08.440
Yeah, it's getting really—

00:00:08.440 --> 00:00:09.730
It's <i>okay</i>.

00:00:13.610 --> 00:00:15.610
Not that I understand.

00:00:17.810 --> 00:00:20.300
Hey, can we end practice, now?

00:00:20.300 --> 00:00:22.500
I have something important 
to talk to you about.

00:00:22.500 --> 00:00:24.260
Could you stop already?

00:00:24.260 --> 00:00:26.740
You keep groaning and moaning.

00:00:28.850 --> 00:00:31.740
Could <i>you</i> stop?

00:00:31.740 --> 00:00:34.980
You need to know your place.

00:00:35.620 --> 00:00:36.460
What are you—

00:00:36.460 --> 00:00:38.010
Come on, guys.

00:00:38.340 --> 00:00:39.140
Hibiki.

00:00:39.140 --> 00:00:40.640
Y-Yes?

00:00:40.640 --> 00:00:44.450
I hear you were cheating on me 
with that shrimp over there.

00:00:44.450 --> 00:00:47.240
How could you be such a skirt-chaser?

00:00:47.240 --> 00:00:51.650
But I'm taller than you, Koume-chan.

00:00:51.650 --> 00:00:53.180
Don't call me Koume-chan!

00:00:53.610 --> 00:00:57.210
And don't you dare slander me, you coward.

00:00:57.210 --> 00:01:00.140
Where exactly did you hear about that?

00:01:00.570 --> 00:01:03.180
You've got some nerve, Hibiki.

00:01:03.180 --> 00:01:04.660
I didn't "hear" it from anywhere.

00:01:04.660 --> 00:01:08.420
They messaged me just to rub 
it in my face yesterday!

00:01:08.780 --> 00:01:10.870
It's a battle of women.

00:01:10.870 --> 00:01:12.050
How exciting.

00:01:12.430 --> 00:01:13.620
You messaged her?

00:01:13.620 --> 00:01:14.840
I did.

00:01:14.840 --> 00:01:18.430
I thought I'd cool her hot head a little.

00:01:19.210 --> 00:01:24.140
I needed to make sure she knew 
you were taking care of <i>us</i> now.

00:01:25.330 --> 00:01:28.150
Kyo-nii's friends with all of us.

00:01:28.150 --> 00:01:28.980
Huh?

00:01:28.980 --> 00:01:30.020
What are you talking about?

00:01:30.020 --> 00:01:32.580
You guys are just toys to him.

00:01:32.580 --> 00:01:33.480
Toys!

00:01:33.480 --> 00:01:36.030
All right, we're going to 
have an important talk now.

00:01:36.030 --> 00:01:38.030
Practice is over!

00:01:38.710 --> 00:01:40.390
K-Kyo-san...

00:01:48.900 --> 00:01:50.410
Hey, Kiriyume...

00:01:51.860 --> 00:01:52.620
Yes?

00:01:52.620 --> 00:01:55.220
Did you finally decide to end practice?

00:01:56.300 --> 00:01:59.370
Sorry, this is important.

00:01:59.370 --> 00:02:01.100
Could you leave for now?

00:02:01.470 --> 00:02:03.140
Say what?

00:02:03.140 --> 00:02:05.880
I don't want you interrupting practice.

00:02:05.880 --> 00:02:08.670
We have a concert coming up.

00:02:08.670 --> 00:02:10.040
Interrupting?

00:02:10.040 --> 00:02:12.780
How could you say that, 
after you cheated on me?

00:02:12.780 --> 00:02:15.190
Is that really how you 
behave to your true wife?

00:02:15.190 --> 00:02:16.070
You aren't my true wife.

00:02:17.440 --> 00:02:21.910
I admire you deeply as an illustrator.

00:02:21.910 --> 00:02:23.920
And you're a precious partner.

00:02:23.920 --> 00:02:26.450
But that's not our relationship.

00:02:31.340 --> 00:02:33.790
How does it feel to wake up from your dream?

00:02:41.660 --> 00:02:42.890
Hibiki...

00:02:43.500 --> 00:02:45.040
Hibiki, you...

00:02:45.040 --> 00:02:48.020
You dumbass!

00:02:49.010 --> 00:02:50.130
Ouch.

00:02:50.130 --> 00:02:50.850
Kiriyume.

00:02:51.320 --> 00:02:52.480
Kiryu-sama!

00:03:00.230 --> 00:03:01.450
Kyo-nii,

00:03:03.770 --> 00:03:06.200
want to practice once more?

00:03:08.260 --> 00:03:09.830
Yeah, let's.

00:03:10.430 --> 00:03:13.080
Okay, let's take it from the top.

00:03:13.080 --> 00:03:14.960
O-Okay.

00:04:54.940 --> 00:04:59.750
Seems you had a lot of fun 
playing with three girls.

00:05:00.430 --> 00:05:08.230
Maybe this is uncalled-for, but if I led 
you on with something I said, I apologize.

00:05:08.810 --> 00:05:09.910
I'm truly sorry.

00:05:11.150 --> 00:05:13.050
Whatever, I get it.

00:05:13.050 --> 00:05:17.670
I don't matter to you at all, do I?

00:05:18.100 --> 00:05:19.650
That's not true.

00:05:19.650 --> 00:05:22.470
It was your illustrations that inspired me to

00:05:22.470 --> 00:05:27.180
work harder on my music 
all this time, Kiriyume.

00:05:27.800 --> 00:05:31.680
And now you're obsessed 
with those other three.

00:05:33.340 --> 00:05:34.020
Yeah.

00:05:34.620 --> 00:05:40.440
I'll admit that I'm just as inspired by 
the music that Lien de Famille makes.

00:05:41.940 --> 00:05:47.070
But worlds you paint are on a different 
wavelength from the others.

00:05:47.070 --> 00:05:49.950
I can't compare and tell you 
which one is more important.

00:05:50.320 --> 00:05:53.700
All I can say is that you're 
both about as important to me.

00:05:55.770 --> 00:05:57.710
So the art isn't enough.

00:05:57.710 --> 00:05:59.870
It's not that it isn't enough.

00:06:00.670 --> 00:06:04.030
I think it's just that I can't think about 
things without thinking about music.

00:06:04.530 --> 00:06:07.970
It's just that I absolutely love it.

00:06:09.470 --> 00:06:14.330
The awesome, heart-warming, 
moving sound of a band.

00:06:18.030 --> 00:06:24.210
It's true that I wanted to do art 
for you because I liked your music.

00:06:24.740 --> 00:06:28.990
I don't think I could have finished 
any of my art without your music.

00:06:29.390 --> 00:06:30.470
Thanks.

00:06:30.470 --> 00:06:34.670
So you'll give me permission 
to work with Jun and the others?

00:06:34.670 --> 00:06:35.820
Say what?

00:06:35.820 --> 00:06:37.530
Why would I?

00:06:37.530 --> 00:06:38.370
Huh?

00:06:38.370 --> 00:06:42.470
You need someone to play 
your music live, right?

00:06:42.470 --> 00:06:43.630
I get that.

00:06:44.070 --> 00:06:45.990
I'll do that, too, then.

00:06:46.990 --> 00:06:50.010
I'm making my own band.

00:06:52.020 --> 00:06:54.380
You're "making" your own band?

00:06:54.380 --> 00:06:56.620
Your own band? With just yourself?

00:06:56.620 --> 00:06:57.930
That's right.

00:06:57.930 --> 00:07:01.770
That way I can make you mine 
with my music and my art.

00:07:02.850 --> 00:07:06.480
I'll make you forget about those shrimps!

00:07:06.480 --> 00:07:08.030
When you say you're "making" a band,

00:07:08.030 --> 00:07:11.460
you mean you're going to 
play instruments and sing?

00:07:11.460 --> 00:07:12.950
Of course not.

00:07:13.460 --> 00:07:15.660
How would I do my drawings, then?

00:07:16.370 --> 00:07:21.100
I thought the concert performance we 
held on the island was pretty workable.

00:07:21.100 --> 00:07:25.000
Where I draw along with the music.

00:07:25.000 --> 00:07:26.860
So then you'll...

00:07:26.030 --> 00:07:29.410
But I refuse to play with those three.

00:07:31.170 --> 00:07:35.980
But if you don't want to work with them, 
what are you going to do for members?

00:07:37.640 --> 00:07:39.860
Yuzuha, you're pretty good 
at singing, aren't you?

00:07:39.860 --> 00:07:40.930
Sing for us.

00:07:40.930 --> 00:07:42.170
Sure.

00:07:42.170 --> 00:07:43.400
That sounds fun.

00:07:43.400 --> 00:07:45.660
B-But what about accompaniment?

00:07:46.940 --> 00:07:48.330
Let's see...

00:07:48.330 --> 00:07:52.410
I guess it'll look silly 
without an instrument or two.

00:07:53.250 --> 00:07:54.430
Oh, I know.

00:07:55.160 --> 00:07:58.410
I guess <i>she'll</i> do.

00:07:59.860 --> 00:08:00.650
She?

00:08:12.620 --> 00:08:15.430
So, will you give me an answer?

00:08:16.230 --> 00:08:18.050
I'm starting a band.

00:08:18.050 --> 00:08:23.110
You're going to join to play 
piano or keyboard or whatever.

00:08:23.110 --> 00:08:23.810
Okay?

00:08:24.280 --> 00:08:28.440
How on Earth do you reach that conclusion?

00:08:28.810 --> 00:08:34.090
I'm honestly curious, did you come 
here <i>actually</i> thinking I'd do it?

00:08:34.930 --> 00:08:38.200
What idiot would turn down 
an invitation from <i>me</i>?

00:08:38.570 --> 00:08:44.160
That question alone gives me enough reason 
to throw salt at you and kick you out.

00:08:44.160 --> 00:08:46.470
Watch it. Mind your words.

00:08:46.470 --> 00:08:48.840
I could disinvite you, you know.

00:08:59.930 --> 00:09:00.820
Fine.

00:09:00.820 --> 00:09:01.600
I'll join.

00:09:03.230 --> 00:09:04.500
Good.

00:09:04.500 --> 00:09:06.780
Well then, I'm done for today.

00:09:06.780 --> 00:09:08.230
I'll be going.

00:09:10.620 --> 00:09:11.230
Hibiki...

00:09:11.230 --> 00:09:12.590
Y-Yes?

00:09:12.590 --> 00:09:15.360
I'll be performing at the next concert.

00:09:15.360 --> 00:09:16.610
What?

00:09:17.030 --> 00:09:21.270
And we're going to take the 
shrimp band's entire audience.

00:09:21.270 --> 00:09:24.370
With my godly performance.

00:09:24.370 --> 00:09:28.660
No matter how good my art may be, I can't 
have the performance being terrible.

00:09:28.660 --> 00:09:31.160
You better come practiced.

00:09:31.160 --> 00:09:32.170
Shut up.

00:09:32.170 --> 00:09:35.100
Just go away and give me back my peace.

00:09:37.820 --> 00:09:39.760
I didn't think you'd accept it.

00:09:40.080 --> 00:09:42.220
Why did you agree to it?

00:09:42.220 --> 00:09:44.270
For just one reason.

00:09:44.810 --> 00:09:45.770
To watch her.

00:09:45.770 --> 00:09:47.140
T-To watch her?

00:09:47.140 --> 00:09:50.620
There's no telling what that 
girl might do. I'm worried.

00:09:50.620 --> 00:09:54.480
I thought it'd be better to keep 
her nearby and under control.

00:09:55.100 --> 00:09:58.860
But do you really want to go 
through all that trouble for me?

00:09:58.860 --> 00:10:02.340
I-I'm not doing it for your sake.

00:10:02.340 --> 00:10:04.730
I don't need that from you.

00:10:04.730 --> 00:10:12.750
Besides, it's not like I don't want to 
show you that I can actually do music.

00:10:14.130 --> 00:10:16.850
Th-There, we're done talking.

00:10:16.850 --> 00:10:18.650
I'm really tired all of a sudden.

00:10:18.650 --> 00:10:21.470
Bring me something cold, Onii-chan.

00:10:22.260 --> 00:10:23.010
Okay.

00:10:29.750 --> 00:10:34.110
<i>Though I already knew Kurumi's
working really hard on the piano.</i>

00:10:38.530 --> 00:10:41.660
A battle of bands with us? 
Who do they think they are?

00:10:42.010 --> 00:10:46.050
Is Koume-chan really angry at us?

00:10:46.580 --> 00:10:48.950
It sounds kind of fun, though.

00:10:48.950 --> 00:10:52.670
Sorry, they might cause some trouble 
for you guys at the next concert

00:10:53.500 --> 00:10:54.710
Not at all.

00:10:54.710 --> 00:10:57.020
It's not your fault, Kyo-san.

00:10:57.020 --> 00:10:57.860
Yeah.

00:10:57.860 --> 00:11:00.230
It's that little girl being a diva.

00:11:00.230 --> 00:11:05.180
All we have to do is accept her 
challenge and beat her down.

00:11:05.180 --> 00:11:06.430
That's all.

00:11:07.070 --> 00:11:08.420
You're right.

00:11:08.420 --> 00:11:10.660
We don't have time until the next concert.

00:11:10.660 --> 00:11:15.190
I don't know if Kiriyume's band will 
ever be presentable on the stage,

00:11:15.560 --> 00:11:19.950
but if it really ends up like the 
performance she's hoping for,

00:11:19.950 --> 00:11:23.200
it might give the audience something new.

00:11:23.700 --> 00:11:26.530
We should be as prepared as we can.

00:11:26.530 --> 00:11:28.510
Kyo-nii's enjoying this.

00:11:29.590 --> 00:11:32.490
I can't wait for the band 
battle with Kiriyume.

00:11:32.490 --> 00:11:34.960
We have to do our best.

00:11:34.960 --> 00:11:36.800
Yeah. We do.

00:11:36.800 --> 00:11:39.220
Oh, jeez.

00:11:39.220 --> 00:11:44.760
I never knew there'd actually be a 
girl who was a god on Soryu Island,

00:11:44.760 --> 00:11:47.720
but she's just as exhausting 
when she's here, too.

00:11:49.470 --> 00:11:50.590
She is.

00:11:52.230 --> 00:11:57.070
I do envy her for that, though.

00:11:57.070 --> 00:12:01.730
She's decisive enough to decide everything 
for herself and try to make things happen.

00:12:01.730 --> 00:12:03.410
That's kind of awesome.

00:12:05.050 --> 00:12:06.600
That's true.

00:12:06.600 --> 00:12:10.010
I can't decide anything for myself.

00:12:10.010 --> 00:12:12.330
I keep troubling you.

00:12:12.330 --> 00:12:13.620
No way.

00:12:14.110 --> 00:12:16.330
I never felt like you were troubling me.

00:12:17.380 --> 00:12:20.340
No, I have too many problems.

00:12:22.220 --> 00:12:26.600
The band can't get anything done without you.

00:12:26.600 --> 00:12:29.220
And my research assignment...

00:12:35.450 --> 00:12:37.690
The research assignment, huh?

00:12:38.000 --> 00:12:43.810
I was so shocked by Kiriyume starting a 
band that I'd totally forgot about it.

00:12:43.810 --> 00:12:46.620
I want to help her, but...

00:12:51.710 --> 00:12:53.360
<i>Is this Kyo-san?</i>

00:12:53.360 --> 00:12:54.320
Jun.

00:12:54.320 --> 00:12:56.460
<i>Sorry to call you so late.</i>

00:12:56.460 --> 00:12:57.340
Nah.

00:12:57.340 --> 00:12:58.460
It's totally fine.

00:12:59.140 --> 00:13:05.090
I've thought of something I want 
to do for the research assignment.

00:13:05.090 --> 00:13:06.110
<i>Really?</i>

00:13:06.110 --> 00:13:07.100
Yes.

00:13:07.100 --> 00:13:09.970
<i>So what have you decided to do?</i>

00:13:11.020 --> 00:13:12.720
Um, I...

00:13:13.220 --> 00:13:15.290
I want to try writing a song.

00:13:15.290 --> 00:13:16.310
<i>A song?</i>

00:13:16.310 --> 00:13:17.350
Yes.

00:13:17.350 --> 00:13:20.820
The three of us had the opportunity 
to write lyrics together,

00:13:20.820 --> 00:13:26.570
but I want to try start writing the music 
and finishing a song all by myself.

00:13:26.570 --> 00:13:32.210
If you asked me what I'm any good at, 
music is the only thing I could think of.

00:13:32.740 --> 00:13:35.890
Music is what I want to work at right now.

00:13:35.890 --> 00:13:37.040
So I figured....

00:13:37.510 --> 00:13:39.420
I'll support you every way I can.

00:13:39.740 --> 00:13:42.250
Th-Thank you.

00:13:42.250 --> 00:13:46.090
But I don't know where to begin.

00:13:46.090 --> 00:13:47.630
So I'm nervous.

00:13:47.970 --> 00:13:50.120
That's how it is for everyone at first.

00:13:50.120 --> 00:13:51.680
I was, too.

00:13:51.680 --> 00:13:53.800
<i>You were?</i>

00:13:53.800 --> 00:13:54.600
Yeah.

00:13:54.600 --> 00:13:57.100
But I promise you'll get the hang of it.

00:13:57.100 --> 00:14:02.110
Work hard at it, and it'll become 
a treasure within you forever.

00:14:02.730 --> 00:14:06.820
So I'd like to help you take the first step.

00:14:07.330 --> 00:14:11.380
So that you can have your own treasure.

00:14:12.630 --> 00:14:13.990
Kyo-san...

00:14:14.620 --> 00:14:16.900
Thank you so much.

00:14:16.900 --> 00:14:18.420
But I'm sorry,

00:14:18.420 --> 00:14:23.000
I've caused you even more trouble when 
we have our band battle with Koume-chan.

00:14:23.000 --> 00:14:27.620
No, in fact, let's premiere your song 
at the concert at the end of the month.

00:14:28.820 --> 00:14:31.400
We can show off even more of

00:14:31.400 --> 00:14:34.890
Lien de Famille's awesomeness if we 
tell them that you wrote the song.

00:14:35.330 --> 00:14:38.770
It'd be our most powerful weapon 
competing against Kiriyume.

00:14:41.330 --> 00:14:44.080
I'm going to do my best, Kyo-san.

00:14:44.080 --> 00:14:46.890
I'm always dependent on you right now,

00:14:46.890 --> 00:14:50.060
but I'm going to move forward, 
even if it takes time.

00:14:56.130 --> 00:14:57.910
All right, let's start.

00:14:58.450 --> 00:15:02.330
I'll provide my humble advice 
for Jun's research assignment.

00:15:02.730 --> 00:15:04.590
Th-Thank you.

00:15:05.000 --> 00:15:09.210
Jumping right in, what do you 
think makes music sound musical?

00:15:09.210 --> 00:15:10.990
What makes it musical?

00:15:12.420 --> 00:15:15.400
Melody, lyrics, and rhythm.

00:15:15.400 --> 00:15:19.850
Those are the three things you need 
for an orthodox piece of music.

00:15:19.850 --> 00:15:20.980
Oh.

00:15:20.980 --> 00:15:23.890
I thought it'd be more complicated than that.

00:15:23.890 --> 00:15:24.690
Right.

00:15:24.690 --> 00:15:27.860
When you think of it that way, 
it's not that complicated.

00:15:28.450 --> 00:15:32.360
So let's pick one of those 
three things to start with.

00:15:32.360 --> 00:15:34.540
You can start with any of them?

00:15:34.540 --> 00:15:35.200
Yup.

00:15:35.200 --> 00:15:39.870
You can start anywhere, but I think 
it's easiest to start with a melody.

00:15:40.410 --> 00:15:43.020
Of course, it differs from person to person.

00:15:43.020 --> 00:15:46.500
But I don't know how to write a melody.

00:15:48.380 --> 00:15:52.070
Jun, could you try humming a little?

00:15:52.070 --> 00:15:53.950
Humming?

00:15:53.950 --> 00:15:54.760
Yeah.

00:16:01.230 --> 00:16:03.740
There, that's one option.

00:16:04.370 --> 00:16:06.660
Let's play that back.

00:16:09.030 --> 00:16:11.530
Th-That's all we need?

00:16:11.530 --> 00:16:13.150
I was just humming.

00:16:13.590 --> 00:16:15.760
All you need is some humming.

00:16:15.760 --> 00:16:21.040
Let's do this a few more times, 
and pick the best one as the main motif.

00:16:22.150 --> 00:16:24.790
I think I can hum, too.

00:16:24.790 --> 00:16:28.450
Kyo, this doesn't sound like making
music as much as it sounds like

00:16:28.450 --> 00:16:31.800
doing stuff until something
happens to sound good by accident.

00:16:32.130 --> 00:16:33.950
That's exactly right.

00:16:33.950 --> 00:16:36.300
A flash of inspiration is incidental, after all.

00:16:36.650 --> 00:16:39.290
So it's more efficient to increase your odds

00:16:39.290 --> 00:16:43.380
of making an accident than to 
overthink it and freak out.

00:16:43.850 --> 00:16:49.320
Do you actually not need to do 
difficult studying to make music?

00:16:49.780 --> 00:16:51.320
You can do it without studying.

00:16:51.640 --> 00:16:57.040
What's really hard is to actually get 
started after you decide to do it,

00:16:57.040 --> 00:17:00.830
and to stick with it until it's done.

00:17:00.830 --> 00:17:04.830
So in my mind, your song 
was already done

00:17:05.960 --> 00:17:08.960
the moment you decided you wanted to do it.

00:17:15.020 --> 00:17:18.940
All right, let's continue recording 
our humming for a while.

00:17:18.940 --> 00:17:21.220
Okay, I'll try.

00:17:37.740 --> 00:17:41.800
Hey, Jun, is it just me, 
or is it getting weirder?

00:17:41.800 --> 00:17:44.620
I think your first one was the most song-like.

00:17:45.730 --> 00:17:47.500
Yeah, I think so, too.

00:17:47.500 --> 00:17:50.370
I think you're feeling too pressured.

00:17:50.370 --> 00:17:52.870
You're trying too hard to make something good

00:17:52.870 --> 00:17:56.010
that you've put a lid on your 
ability to do things by chance.

00:17:59.930 --> 00:18:03.630
It'd be better if you could 
hum something more naturally.

00:18:03.630 --> 00:18:04.750
Kyo-nii.

00:18:05.260 --> 00:18:08.770
What makes you want to hum?

00:18:08.770 --> 00:18:10.490
Let's see...

00:18:10.490 --> 00:18:14.330
When I'm in a really good 
mood, and I'm relaxed.

00:18:15.150 --> 00:18:17.740
Oh, like when I'm taking a bath.

00:18:32.750 --> 00:18:35.420
H-How did this happen?

00:18:36.470 --> 00:18:40.930
You said you hum when you take a bath.

00:18:40.930 --> 00:18:43.630
But why do <i>I</i> need to be here?

00:18:43.630 --> 00:18:48.640
How else can we figure out if it's 
good or not when she starts humming?

00:18:50.220 --> 00:18:52.400
It's fun taking a bath with the four of us.

00:18:52.400 --> 00:18:55.610
Jun-tan, do you think you can hum?

00:18:55.610 --> 00:18:56.830
Don't do that, Sora.

00:18:56.830 --> 00:18:59.790
You're going to put pressure on her again.

00:19:00.620 --> 00:19:02.550
Thanks, you two.

00:19:02.550 --> 00:19:07.790
I'll do my best to come up with something 
naturally and not overthink it.

00:19:08.450 --> 00:19:09.940
I'm home.

00:19:10.500 --> 00:19:14.290
Wearing this reminds me of Soryu Island.

00:19:15.870 --> 00:19:20.300
The food was delicious 
and the naps were great.

00:19:20.300 --> 00:19:23.170
Yeah, it was so much fun.

00:19:23.170 --> 00:19:24.760
I hope we can go again.

00:19:39.490 --> 00:19:40.700
That one.

00:19:40.700 --> 00:19:42.110
That one was really good.

00:19:43.060 --> 00:19:46.620
Use that one as a motif, 
and we can make a masterpiece.

00:19:47.350 --> 00:19:48.100
Record it.

00:19:48.100 --> 00:19:50.580
Record it before we forget.

00:19:50.580 --> 00:19:51.410
O-Okay.

00:19:56.710 --> 00:20:00.260
Why are you making so much noise in the bath?

00:20:07.150 --> 00:20:11.310
Wh-Wh-What are you doing?!

00:20:12.610 --> 00:20:15.310
Helping Jun-tan make music.

00:20:16.450 --> 00:20:17.440
I'm home.

00:20:24.070 --> 00:20:26.070
So Kiriyume did?

00:20:26.460 --> 00:20:27.200
Yeah.

00:20:27.810 --> 00:20:30.330
She said we're going to put on a huge show with

00:20:30.330 --> 00:20:32.710
this piece and give
you a run for your money.

00:20:33.180 --> 00:20:35.210
<i>Is she holding a grudge?</i>

00:20:36.940 --> 00:20:41.610
I can play it now, but I don't know.

00:20:42.970 --> 00:20:45.340
I heard Aigae-san's singing.

00:20:45.980 --> 00:20:50.540
With her vocals, and with 
the drawing onstage,

00:20:50.540 --> 00:20:53.350
I feel like I'm going to be the weakest act.

00:20:54.100 --> 00:20:57.860
Maybe it's hard to keep up with just piano.

00:21:01.340 --> 00:21:03.180
Hey, in that case...

00:21:04.130 --> 00:21:07.870
Why don't you make a backing 
track to add more sound?

00:21:07.870 --> 00:21:11.680
Sure, if I could do such 
a thing, but I can't.

00:21:11.680 --> 00:21:12.940
I'll help you.

00:21:12.940 --> 00:21:13.750
What?

00:21:14.140 --> 00:21:15.720
What are you talking about?

00:21:15.720 --> 00:21:20.370
Helping me is one thing, but we're trying
to pick a fight with Jun and the others.

00:21:21.260 --> 00:21:23.510
I get that, but...

00:21:23.850 --> 00:21:29.010
For once, I want to help 
you out, as your brother.

00:21:33.310 --> 00:21:36.380
Onii-chan, you're kind of being a showoff.

00:23:21.480 --> 00:23:25.000
<b>Band Battles and Melodies</b>

00:23:25.820 --> 00:23:41.500
<b>#12: Can't Help but Love the Music</b>

00:23:26.260 --> 00:23:29.760
We're going to knock their 
socks off at the band battle.

00:23:29.760 --> 00:23:32.840
They'd better repent.

00:23:32.840 --> 00:23:36.650
I hope we raise the roof at the concert.
